.TH SOC-OTA-AGENT 1 "October 2026" "OTA-Pulse" "OTA-Pulse Manual"
.SH NAME
soc-ota-agent, otapulse \- OTA-Pulse device update agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soc-ota-agent
[\fIglobal options\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIcommand options\fR]
.br
.B otapulse
(same program, alternative name)
.SH DESCRIPTION
The agent runs on the device. In daemon mode it polls the OTA-Pulse backend for deployments, downloads
and installs signed root file system artifacts into the inactive A/B slot, reports status and inventory,
and commits the update once the new slot has booted and passed its health checks, or reports the failure
after a rollback.
.PP
The package configures the agent for \fBbootloader compatibility mode\fR (\fBBootEnvMode\fR is
\fBbootloader\fR in \fI/etc/otapulse/otapulse.conf\fR): the bootloader integration of the board (U-Boot or
GRUB) owns the boot-slot flag, the boot counter and the rollback. The agent only writes the
bootloader environment through its tools (\fBfw_setenv\fR, or the GRUB environment tools of the image). It
never switches the slot by itself and never falls back to a file based boot environment. If the bootloader
environment cannot be read, the agent refuses to run and logs the reason.
.PP
\fBotapulse-data-seed.service\fR runs before the agent. It copies \fI/etc/otapulse/device_type\fR to
\fI/data/otapulse/device_type\fR on the first start and verifies it on every later start. If the data
partition carries a different device type, the service fails and the agent does not start. The service also
refuses to run when \fI/data\fR is not a mount point.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Run the update daemon. This is what the systemd unit \fBsoc-ota-agent.service\fR starts.
.TP
.B show-artifact
Print the name of the installed artifact.
.TP
.B show-provides
Print the provides data of the installed artifact.
.TP
.B commit
Commit an installed update.
.TP
.B rollback
Roll back an installed update that has not been committed.
.PP
Run \fBsoc-ota-agent --help\fR for the complete list of commands and options of the installed version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/otapulse/otapulse.conf
Configuration (JSON). Contains no credentials as shipped. \fBServerURL\fR, \fBRootfsPartA\fR and
\fBRootfsPartB\fR have to be set for the image.
.TP
.I /etc/otapulse/boot_mode
Contains the word \fBbootloader\fR. The update state scripts read it and do nothing in this mode.
.TP
.I /etc/otapulse/device_type, /var/lib/otapulse/device_type
Device type that artifacts are checked against.
.TP
.I /data/otapulse/otapulse.conf
Credentials written by \fBsoc-ota-provision\fR(1). Loaded as a fallback configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/share/otapulse/state-scripts/
State scripts that are embedded into artifacts.
.TP
.I /etc/soc-monitoring/signing-keys/active/
Public keys used to verify artifact signatures. Artifact verification is required.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR soc-ota-provision (1),
.BR socmond (1)
